{"agent":"bugs-identity","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new adoption match compares the path recorded in the event against `W.store_path(repo, here.path)`, i.e. the *store* path of the current worktree, while the docstring added in the same hunk states that `worktree.adopted` \"names the tree's path\" — the specific tree that was adopted. These are only equal if `store_path` is the identity on `here.path`; the fact that it takes `repo` indicates it resolves the shared store for the worktree. Because the event log/hooks are shared across the project's worktrees, `stored` is the same value for every linked worktree of the repo, whereas adoptions are recorded per tree. Concretely: parent P (which always passes `--agent P`) claims from its harness tree T, emitting `worktree.adopted{path: T, agent: P}`; agent C then claims its own linked worktree W, emitting `worktree.adopted{path: W, agent: C}`. When C later runs any command from W, `own = tree_agent_ids(W)` does not contain C (C never wrote under W's derived name), `stored = store_path(W)` equals T's store, P's adoption matches (`e.agent != C`, so `adopter = P`), and C's own adoption of W (`path: W != stored`) is never matched — so `foreign_tree_owner` returns `P`. C is told its own claimed tree belongs to the parent, so the next `ddflow --agent C claim` creates yet another tree instead of using W, and gate/review/merge for C's items are answered as from the primary. The comparison must be against the tree's own path (`here.path`), not the shared store path, for the per-tree adoption semantics the comment and README describe.","digest":"6a6eab1884facc77","location":"ddflow/services/tree_owner.py — `stored = W.store_path(repo, here.path)` / `e.data.get(\"path\") == stored`","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/tree_owner.py — `stored = W.store_path(repo, here.path)` / `e.data.get(\"path\") == stored`"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":7305,"diff_sha":"7da0d7a0e8175229002654e5e3fd8f7f8db82bd100696041f274ecaba05a8f62","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-fix-identity-attribution","elapsed_s":287.2,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/tree_owner.py — `stored = W.store_path(repo, here.path)` / `e.data.get(\"path\") == stored`"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e0a74df491df08f32839f1825","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":10968,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-identity-attribution","ts":"2026-10-02T18:28:53.651122Z"}
